{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1172217-spirit-files-wta","id":1172217,"title":"Spirit Files: WTA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-01T02:33:01-08:00","id":1172217,"title":"Spirit Files: WTA","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">First Hello To all the Roll players in the Forum!<br /> <br /> This is my first time Using a Forum to achieve my goal for this year. I am working all year (2018) to make 2 or 3 submissions for Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> I have been truly intrigued by Spirits in cWOD Driving my DrivethurRPG bill up quite a bit.</span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I</span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> am</span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> looking for resources about spirits or even ideas?<br /> <br /> <br /> So currently have most the book in Spirits by Type (</span></span>http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf\u200b) fan made spirit long<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">My Goal is to move them from 5 Stats (Rage, Gnosis, Willpower, Essence/power, Charms) to Fullness like All other beings in cWoD!<br /> <br /> This is a big project so If anyone shares my Vision or has words of enourgement. let me know!<br /> <br /> If anyone is also a big Wraith player i am not as Fimilar with that game Want to learn more!</span></span> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T03:53:11-08:00","id":1172224,"title":"","content":"Happy new year <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23653\" data-vbnamecard=\"23653\">Alstonjc</a><br /> I did make a try to change spirit stuff as you do and I find it quite interesting to share thought with you on the subject.<br /> The thing is that spirits are not like normal people so giving them full 9 attributes and health levels will take away their spiritual id.<br /> But if you you lett them simplified up to 5 stats makes them look shallow.<br /> My idea was to make a mix of both.<br /> For instance spirits must be devided by levels, which so far in Apocalypse its flux in stat representation.<br /> There must be a list that will give indications on how powerful a spirit level can be and what gifts it can teach.<br /> There can be a distinction between spirits that have spiritual health level (without woundpenalties) like animal spirits and spirits that take damage directly in essence like elementals.<br /> The core of this idea is to make unique spirit classes.<br /> <br /> What do you think about it as a starting idea ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 01-01-2018, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T09:02:18-08:00","id":1172274,"title":"","content":"My take on spirits would be a bit different than expanding on rare attributes. I think the current system works really well for the theme.<br /> I'd rather expand their nature in other ways, like literaly their Nature, Elemental Affinity, such things. Bygone Bestiary has a few ideas about how an Elemental Affinity corresponds with different Natures.<br /> Since spirits mostly have a Nature but a differing Demeanor is rare (trickster spirits, maybe), this would be the main focus.<br /> There could be a selection of Elemental and more specialized Nature Charms, to flesh out the powers of a spirit. Also, different Natures, Affinities (think of more than the classical elements, there are the weaver and wyrm elementals too and a lot of other possibilities) would add different mechanics (like, ways to recover Gnosis Points, Essence or Rage).<br /> I never liked that spirits have to spend Essence to fuel their charms, because using your very life force to do stuff is quite costly. Gnosis- and Rage-Points for Charms might be more appropriate. This way, spirits could maybe even evolve into playable characters, without the need to slumber after every scene.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just had the thought of connecting Rage Points to an (Elemental) Affinity, while Gnosis Points would be recovered by acting out your Nature. This way, a Spirit that is Rage dependent would be much more primal, while a Gnosis dependent Spirit could show a much more sophisticated personality.<br /> <br /> Of course Rage Points would be used for aggressive Charms, dealing damage or wrecking stuff, physical changes like growing even more/bigger claws and teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","user":"TheVarulfen","date":". 01-01-2018, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T02:26:50-08:00","id":1173182,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\">Story Letter</a> I really Like your Idea!!!</b><br /> <br /> First Happy New year!!<br /> <br /> I agree with you Spirits are not the Like their flesh Counterparts. But I am thinking about my submission too. I don't want to be so far different from the cannon game with too many new concepts to learn.<br /> <br /> I am also using some of Wraith as a template.<br /> <br /> But I want to hear more I am starting with an Earth Elemental! what would be your make of it with your idea?<br /> (I have started and if I use something of yours I would need your information to give you credit even as a collaborator if you don't mind)<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for reading my post and taking time to answer!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":23653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","user":"Alstonjc","date":". 01-04-2018, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T02:46:32-08:00","id":1173185,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen\">TheVarulfen</a> I have never thought of this!</b><br /> <br /> First Happy New year!!<br /> <br /> YES! I agree i think that is a part I realized but never made a part of my questions I must answer!<br /> <br /> How per there nature do the regain Gnosis or Rage (If i keep the names)? <br /> <br /> Drive and mindset is very important to me! so the nature or affinity.<br /> <br /> Why does the spirit help you? or What is it persived goal or purpose? or What actions does this drive?<br /> <br /> This really got me thinking! I have the book to so i can look there as well!<br /> <br /> But I want to hear more I am starting with an Earth Elemental! what would be your make of it with your idea?<br /> (I have started and if I use something of yours I would need your information to give you credit even as a collaborator if you don't mind)<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for reading my post and taking time to answer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T08:12:06-08:00","id":1173220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alstonjc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1172217-spirit-files-wta?p=1173182#post1173182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\">Story Letter</a> I really Like your Idea!!!</b><br /> <br /> First Happy New year!!<br /> <br /> I agree with you Spirits are not the Like their flesh Counterparts. But I am thinking about my submission too. I don't want to be so far different from the cannon game with too many new concepts to learn.<br /> <br /> I am also using some of Wraith as a template.<br /> <br /> But I want to hear more I am starting with an Earth Elemental! what would be your make of it with your idea?<br /> (I have started and if I use something of yours I would need your information to give you credit even as a collaborator if you don't mind)<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for reading my post and taking time to answer!</div> </div> </div> </div>Earth Elementals are split in three cstegories.<br /> <u><b>a)Light which are spirits of mud and dust</b></u><br /> These spirits are primal and fundamendal in existance and have Willpower, Rage, Gnosis and Essence. When an enemy hurts them they gain direct essence damage but depending of the kind of spirit the difficulty to hit or damage is its willpower (dust), gnosis (mud) or Rage (sandstorm), if the difficulty is Rage the enemy may try to soak damage if he hits the elemental unarmed.<br /> <br /> <u><b>b)Stable spirits of solid ground and rock</b></u><br /> These spirits always have attributes like material encounters with health levels that do not impose wound penalties, these spirits still have Rage, Gnosis an Willpower but are not related to attributes. Instead Rage is the damage they do with earth charms, Gnosis is the power of their mental charms and willpower is their resistance to various powers and their earth manipulating powers. The health levels attributes and skills depend on the size, the shape and the age of the elemental.<br /> Table Elementals can't soak aggravated damage and cannot inflict aggravate damage without the aid of a gift.<br /> <br /> <u><b>c)Hard spirits of primal and unshaken elements</b></u><br /> These are the mightiest Earth elementals around, they are much like Stable Elementals but take damage only from aggravated sources, or from lethal if it exceeds their Willpower rating as their existance its too hard to damage.<br /> They have attributes, skills and health levels and are always armoured (see below)<br /> In order to damage a Hard elemental you must damage it with aggravated damage which the elemental soaks with stamina and armor charm.<br /> Attacks inflicted by hard elementals are always lethal except if they hit with sharpened limbs which do aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Rage Gnosis and Willpower work exactly like Stable Elementals with some additional effects.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Rage rating allows a Hard elemental automatic successes in damage, so an Earth elemental with Rage 5 and 7 strength will roll 2 dice for damage and will add 5 successes.<br /> Willpower acts as automatic defense in soak rolls and mind powers like Rage does in damage. An ellemental with 10 soak and willpower 6 will roll 4 dice for soaking and will add the other 6 as automatic successes. In case of mind attacks the enemy will have to bypass in difficulty the elemental's willpower rating and if contested, well prey that the elemental has low willpower rating.<br /> Gnosis gives automatic successes to all social and mental tests (earth elemental have shaking presence and unshaken memory).<br /> <br /> All earth elementals take essence damage if attacked with aggravated damage. Essence rating is as always the sum of Rage, Gnosis and Willpower.<br /> <br /> Hope it wasn't too complicated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 01-04-2018, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T09:17:11-08:00","id":1173240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alstonjc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1172217-spirit-files-wta?p=1173185#post1173185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen\">TheVarulfen</a> I have never thought of this!</b><br /> <br /> First Happy New year!!<br /> <br /> YES! I agree i think that is a part I realized but never made a part of my questions I must answer!<br /> <br /> How per there nature do the regain Gnosis or Rage (If i keep the names)?<br /> <br /> Drive and mindset is very important to me! so the nature or affinity.<br /> <br /> Why does the spirit help you? or What is it persived goal or purpose? or What actions does this drive?<br /> <br /> This really got me thinking! I have the book to so i can look there as well!<br /> <br /> But I want to hear more I am starting with an Earth Elemental! what would be your make of it with your idea?<br /> (I have started and if I use something of yours I would need your information to give you credit even as a collaborator if you don't mind)<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for reading my post and taking time to answer!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, so Bygone Beastiary lists a bunch of personality archetypes for each element. This would be the one for earth elemental types:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Earth<br /> \u2022 Crystalline idealist<br /> \u2022 Fertile procreator<br /> \u2022 Flowery bon vivant<br /> \u2022 Resolute architect<br /> \u2022 Sheltering caregiver<br /> \u2022 Solid guardian<br /> \u2022 Stony curmudgeon </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking about using Rage and Gnosis like in Werewolf, having a permanent rating and temporary points you spend on Charms and special abilities.<br /> Rage is used for &quot;physical&quot; Charms and abilities. A stone spirit would probably use the Armor-Charm, enhancing their Soak-Ability. This would cost a Rage-Point instead of Essence.<br /> Now, how could a stone spirit regain Rage? It's a bit different than with a Werewolf or the Fera. He would have to do something stone related, like, let's say, slumber in rocky terrain.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Gnosis. This attribute is about metaphysically influencing and perceiving the world around you. This includes other spirits and even physical entities. You spend Gnosis-Points on Charms to influence someones mood or thoughts, for altering an aspect of the world around you. This is different than Willpower, which is used to &quot;physically&quot; change the world (as in, with your hands, claws, feet and so on).<br /> Gnosis could be regained by acting according to your personality type. A &quot;fertile procreator&quot; would regain Gnosis, whenever his actions further some aspect of fertility. Maybe making a region of land fertile for flowers and other plants to grow there.<br /> <br /> Now Willpower. The &quot;physical&quot; stat for spirits. I wouldn't use it to fuel Charms, but the same way that it is used in any other oWOD gamelines. And it is replenished in the same way.<br /> <br /> And last but not least, Essence. This one's your very life force. If it's depleted, you'll fall into slumber for a few decades or even hundreds of years. And you may very well destroyed entirely (I'm imagining eating other spirits to gain power is a thing, like consuming other Fallen in Demon).<br /> That being said, Essence would be a stat, rather than a fix number of health levels. And you could spend it too. If you're in trouble, out of Gnosis or Rage, you could use Essence as a substitute, fuelling your Charms with it and risking to get ever closer to slumber. I'm not sure about how fast Essence should be recovered. This would be a major balancing factor. Maybe it's also possible to trade in Gnosis- and Rage-Points for Essence, thus only healing when acting in accordance to your Nature and Element. (I actually really like where this is going.)<br /> <br /> Hope this helps inspiring you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T17:39:26-08:00","id":1173379,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen\">TheVarulfen</a> &amp; </b><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\">Story Letter</a></b><br /> OMG Thank you for the information! Think this is great I have to look it over when i am not so tired I am new to doing a forum.<br /> <br /> yes it not to hard I am super tired though!<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for reading my post and taking time to answer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T12:18:04-08:00","id":1173810,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the old WoD book about spirits was called <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/28/Axis-Mundi-The-Book-of-Spirits?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Axis Mundi</a>, primarily for Werewolf but also done with Mage in mind. You may also find <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/62211/Inanimae-The-Secret-Way?term=inanim&amp;test_epoch=0\" target=\"_blank\">Inanimae</a> for Changeling useful for ideas about elementals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T06:20:03-08:00","id":1174255,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\">No One of Consequence</a></b><br /> <br /> I have a both of the books!<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for reading my post and taking time to answer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T00:33:10-08:00","id":1194165,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen\">TheVarulfen</a> &amp; </b><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\">Story Letter</a></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>I am working on some writing now I would like to give you credit for your ideas can you send me a Private message with contact information!</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}